#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
"""maelys-cli-man: the manual page of a program built on maelys-cli, in roff
(man(7), section 1), rendered from its own catalog.

usage: maelys-cli-man [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--lang TAG] [--untranslated] PROGRAM [WORD...]

The program is run once, as `PROGRAM [WORD...] describe --format json`, and
its catalog form is the only source: the help is a rendering of describe,
and so is this page. Nothing is written by hand and nothing is guessed.

The page follows the rules of the help, which is for humans too: a hidden
command or a hidden option is never on it, and a command this build cannot
run is marked as such with its reason. EXIT STATUS is the contract's 0, 1
and 2, every command having those three; a stream or a delegate exits with
the status of what it runs. The line under the program's name comes from
`x-maelys-summary`, and the product's guidance (`x-maelys-guidance`) is
prose for humans and agents, never a source of command lines: an agent
builds those from `input`.

The tool runs the product, so it runs where the product runs: a product
cross-compiled for another machine renders its page on that machine, or
from a native build of the same tag. The date defaults to the day of
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH when it is set, to today otherwise; --date fixes it. The
source is the same on Linux and macOS for the same catalog and date.

With --lang TAG the page is in that language when the program declares it:
the catalog form carries the product's tables (`x-maelys-translations`), and
this tool the framework's, generated from i18n/*.tsv as the library's are.
The tag is looked up as the runtime looks it up (RFC 4647, fr-CA finding
fr); a language the program does not declare gives the English page, as
--lang does. A text a table leaves out stays in English, one by one.
--untranslated prints, instead of the page, each text of the page that
stays in English, one per line: what a product's table still lacks.

Validate the result with `mandoc -T lint` or `groff -ww -man -z`.
"""

